1
00:00:40,959 --> 00:00:43,375
[2016 Daejeon]

2
00:00:43,375 --> 00:00:44,792
Here, Sir.

3
00:00:49,542 --> 00:00:51,417
- Thank you.
- Have a nice day.

4
00:00:51,417 --> 00:00:54,084
Thank you. Take care.

5
00:00:58,083 --> 00:01:02,000
[Yun Hee]

6
00:01:03,292 --> 00:01:04,876
- Yeah, Yun Hee?
<i>- Honey,</i>

7
00:01:04,876 --> 00:01:07,167
are you sleeping at the
sleeping quarters tonight?

8
00:01:07,167 --> 00:01:08,834
<i>Afraid so.</i>

9
00:01:08,834 --> 00:01:10,542
When will you get there?

10
00:01:11,459 --> 00:01:13,209
Well,

11
00:01:13,209 --> 00:01:15,125
I'm not sure.

12
00:01:15,125 --> 00:01:16,459
I see.

13
00:01:16,459 --> 00:01:18,375
Why? Is something up?

14
00:01:18,375 --> 00:01:20,417
No, everything's fine.

15
00:01:20,417 --> 00:01:22,125
Just asking.

16
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:26,083
<i>Excuse me, ma'am. I'm from the police.</i>

17
00:01:26,083 --> 00:01:28,584
<i>- Oh, okay.
- It's dangerous here.</i>

18
00:01:28,584 --> 00:01:29,667
<i>- Please move.
- Okay.</i>

19
00:01:29,667 --> 00:01:31,167
What is it?

20
00:01:31,167 --> 00:01:32,918
What's happening there?

21
00:01:32,918 --> 00:01:35,292
Nothing.

22
00:01:35,292 --> 00:01:37,167
Someone had an accident.

23
00:01:37,167 --> 00:01:39,042
Yeah. I'll call you later.

24
00:01:39,042 --> 00:01:40,500
Okay.

25
00:01:46,417 --> 00:01:48,334
<i>The suspect, Lee Geun Sang,</i>

26
00:01:48,334 --> 00:01:51,167
<i>was shot and killed by the police.</i>

27
00:01:51,167 --> 00:01:53,792
<i>His accomplice, Kim Mun Su,</i>

28
00:01:53,792 --> 00:01:56,000
<i>fled the scene and is now on the run.</i>

29
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,042
- I don't know!
- Hold still!

30
00:01:59,042 --> 00:02:01,792
<i>Lieutenant Park, who sustained injury,</i>

31
00:02:01,792 --> 00:02:05,083
<i>passed away at the hospital.</i>

32
00:02:05,083 --> 00:02:07,459
<i>Her partner, Officer Min, was seriously injured</i>

33
00:02:07,459 --> 00:02:10,000
<i>and is now in surgery.</i>

34
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,042
<i>The police has released a public wanted notice…</i>

35
00:02:13,042 --> 00:02:14,876
Please pick up.

36
00:02:14,876 --> 00:02:17,250
<i>and set up checkpoints
along key roads and exits,</i>

37
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:21,334
<i>in case he escaped to areas outside of Daejeon.</i>

38
00:02:24,167 --> 00:02:26,709
<i>Happy birthday, honey.</i>

39
00:02:26,709 --> 00:02:29,459
<i>I know you are too busy to see me,</i>

40
00:02:29,459 --> 00:02:32,042
<i>but I still wanted to give you this cake.</i>

41
00:02:32,709 --> 00:02:34,918
<i>Make a wish before you eat it,</i>

42
00:02:34,918 --> 00:02:38,000
<i>so that we can spend
the next birthday together.</i>

43
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:41,083
<i>Don't skip your meals.</i>

44
00:02:41,083 --> 00:02:42,584
<i>Love, Yun Hee.</i>

45
00:02:47,375 --> 00:02:48,584
Yun Hee.

46
00:02:48,584 --> 00:02:50,792
[Two Missed Calls]

47
00:02:50,792 --> 00:02:51,876
[Yun Hee]

48
00:03:00,167 --> 00:03:03,209
Why is he not picking up?

49
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,083
- Stop gloating.
- See you in the morning.

50
00:03:21,167 --> 00:03:23,542
[Four Missed Calls]

51
00:03:31,292 --> 00:03:33,042
[Yun Hee]

52
00:03:36,500 --> 00:03:38,500
- <i>Honey.</i>
- Yun Hee.

53
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:40,167
Sorry, I missed your call.

54
00:03:40,167 --> 00:03:42,375
<i>I am now…</i>

55
00:03:52,334 --> 00:03:54,834
Yun Hee, what's wrong? What happened?

56
00:03:54,834 --> 00:03:56,167
[Honey]

57
00:03:58,918 --> 00:04:00,792
Yun Hee!

58
00:04:04,042 --> 00:04:06,250
[Honey]

59
00:04:07,042 --> 00:04:10,209
[Honey]

60
00:04:14,876 --> 00:04:16,334
[Seoul Metropolitan Police
National Office Of Investigation]

61
00:04:16,334 --> 00:04:18,209
I can't take it anymore.

62
00:04:18,209 --> 00:04:20,500
My classmate is getting a promotion,

63
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:23,083
and I'm here delivering flowers.

64
00:04:23,083 --> 00:04:26,584
When we graduated the academy
he was well below my level.

65
00:04:26,584 --> 00:04:29,667
We were in different leagues.
And he outranks me now?

66
00:04:29,667 --> 00:04:32,167
- I mean, come on.
- You know the saying.

67
00:04:32,167 --> 00:04:35,292
Beginner's luck doesn't last long.

68
00:04:35,292 --> 00:04:38,083
That's the story of your life.

69
00:04:38,083 --> 00:04:39,959
- Beginner's luck?
- Kidding, just kidding.

70
00:04:39,959 --> 00:04:41,542
Kidding? You think it's funny?

71
00:04:41,542 --> 00:04:44,417
You really think saying that
lets you get away with anything?

72
00:04:44,417 --> 00:04:46,584
- No, I didn't mean-
- Since when did you

73
00:04:46,584 --> 00:04:48,792
become so daring around me?

74
00:04:48,792 --> 00:04:51,584
What does that make you?

75
00:04:51,584 --> 00:04:54,334
You didn't even have beginner's luck!

76
00:04:54,334 --> 00:04:57,667
You were unlucky from the get-go!

77
00:04:57,667 --> 00:04:59,375
You're right.

78
00:04:59,375 --> 00:05:00,959
Oh!

79
00:05:00,959 --> 00:05:03,918
- Chief Koo.
- Hey, Superintendent Chang. Why are you here?

80
00:05:03,918 --> 00:05:07,042
What do you mean by that?
I have the right to be here!

81
00:05:07,042 --> 00:05:11,042
You mean district chiefs
need permission or something?

82
00:05:11,042 --> 00:05:14,542
- Why is this guy so ticked off?
- Well, you know how it is.

83
00:05:14,542 --> 00:05:16,876
Oh wait, did you hear?

84
00:05:16,876 --> 00:05:20,459
Hear what? You didn't say what it is.

85
00:05:20,459 --> 00:05:22,459
How should I know if I heard it

86
00:05:22,459 --> 00:05:25,000
- when I don't even know what it is?
- My goodness.

87
00:05:27,792 --> 00:05:29,125
Well, this is…

88
00:05:39,876 --> 00:05:41,292
My, my.

89
00:05:43,792 --> 00:05:46,292
Oh, dear. Oh, dear.

90
00:05:46,292 --> 00:05:48,500
Son Min A, your first love.

91
00:05:48,500 --> 00:05:50,626
She's come to NOI.

92
00:05:50,626 --> 00:05:52,500
She's the new director.

93
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,876
Oh, dear.

94
00:05:55,876 --> 00:05:58,167
Just a peek, just…

95
00:05:58,167 --> 00:05:59,584
Wait, wait…

96
00:05:59,584 --> 00:06:01,375
What's wrong with me?

97
00:06:01,375 --> 00:06:03,584
What's wrong with me?

98
00:06:03,584 --> 00:06:05,876
Why is my heart beating so fast?

99
00:06:05,876 --> 00:06:09,167
Just calm down, just…

100
00:06:09,167 --> 00:06:11,042
Did you hear?

101
00:06:11,042 --> 00:06:13,459
A new director came to NOI.

102
00:06:13,459 --> 00:06:14,626
A detective bureau?

103
00:06:14,626 --> 00:06:18,334
Yeah. She used to lead
the Narcotics Unit in Busan.

104
00:06:18,334 --> 00:06:20,542
Where do you get such news?

105
00:06:20,542 --> 00:06:23,000
Your friend at NOI told you?

106
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:25,459
Not a friend.

107
00:06:25,459 --> 00:06:28,000
Anyway, her name is Son Min A.

108
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,083
Son Min A?

109
00:06:29,083 --> 00:06:33,584
I think we'll see her quite often
because we're under her command.

110
00:06:35,083 --> 00:06:37,459
- Is something wrong?
- Nothing.

111
00:06:39,876 --> 00:06:41,375
- What was that?
- Did we just hit her?

112
00:06:41,375 --> 00:06:43,876
I think we did. It's bad.

113
00:06:43,876 --> 00:06:45,250
Oh dear…

114
00:06:45,250 --> 00:06:48,542
Are you all right?

115
00:06:48,542 --> 00:06:50,918
Can you stand up?

116
00:06:50,918 --> 00:06:52,083
Were you hit by the car?

117
00:06:52,083 --> 00:06:53,584
Do you even need to ask?

118
00:06:53,584 --> 00:06:56,125
She must be hurt. And she's pregnant.

119
00:06:56,125 --> 00:06:59,375
You should have been careful!
You could have hurt the baby.

120
00:06:59,375 --> 00:07:01,167
Let's get you to a hospital.

121
00:07:01,167 --> 00:07:04,083
I can get there by myself. Just-.

122
00:07:05,959 --> 00:07:07,834
Oh my god.

123
00:07:07,834 --> 00:07:08,876
[Police]

124
00:07:08,876 --> 00:07:11,584
Why? Is something wrong?

125
00:07:15,167 --> 00:07:16,709
No!

126
00:07:17,250 --> 00:07:19,125
I think I'm fine.

127
00:07:19,125 --> 00:07:21,542
- Huh?
- Just get on your way.

128
00:07:21,542 --> 00:07:23,792
- No, you can't-
- Oh, I almost forgot.

129
00:07:23,792 --> 00:07:25,125
Gotta feed my baby.

130
00:07:25,125 --> 00:07:27,250
Wait, wait! You can't!

131
00:07:27,250 --> 00:07:29,083
You might have problems later.

132
00:07:29,083 --> 00:07:31,250
I said I'm fine! Really.

133
00:07:31,250 --> 00:07:33,584
No, you're not fine. Hey, wait!

134
00:07:33,584 --> 00:07:35,918
I'm a police officer. I can't leave you here.

135
00:07:35,918 --> 00:07:38,209
I said I'm fine!

136
00:07:40,209 --> 00:07:41,751
- What is this?
- Lieutenant!

137
00:07:41,751 --> 00:07:42,959
Darn it.

138
00:07:42,959 --> 00:07:44,500
It's a "wrist scam"!

139
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:45,876
I mean, what-

140
00:07:45,876 --> 00:07:49,042
[Wrist scam: A scam involving
staging a traffic injury]

141
00:07:53,209 --> 00:07:55,292
Get up already!

142
00:07:55,292 --> 00:07:56,500
I'm so sorry!

143
00:07:56,500 --> 00:07:58,292
Please let me go!

144
00:07:58,292 --> 00:08:00,542
We'll talk at the station.

145
00:08:00,542 --> 00:08:03,584
I can't. My baby is at home alone.

146
00:08:03,584 --> 00:08:05,876
There's no one to look after her.

147
00:08:05,876 --> 00:08:08,209
- Please, officer!
- She's lying, obviously.

148
00:08:08,959 --> 00:08:10,209
I'm not lying!

149
00:08:10,209 --> 00:08:13,042
Come and see for yourself!

150
00:08:16,375 --> 00:08:19,292
[Laon's Motel]

151
00:08:19,292 --> 00:08:20,667
She wasn't lying.

152
00:08:20,667 --> 00:08:23,334
Oh, oh!

153
00:08:23,334 --> 00:08:25,334
It's okay.

154
00:08:25,334 --> 00:08:28,250
I'm sorry, but can you…

155
00:08:28,250 --> 00:08:32,292
- I gotta feed her.
- Yeah, I'll uncuff you.

156
00:08:32,292 --> 00:08:33,375
It's okay.

157
00:08:33,375 --> 00:08:35,918
Okay, okay.

158
00:08:35,918 --> 00:08:38,959
All right, here.

159
00:08:42,042 --> 00:08:43,417
Okay.

160
00:08:44,375 --> 00:08:47,667
Why so sad?

161
00:08:47,667 --> 00:08:50,584
Mommy's here.

162
00:08:50,584 --> 00:08:53,792
There, there.

163
00:08:54,918 --> 00:08:57,500
Let's eat, okay?

164
00:09:02,876 --> 00:09:04,459
Give it here.

165
00:09:05,417 --> 00:09:07,000
Thank you.

166
00:09:10,751 --> 00:09:12,417
So adorable.

167
00:09:13,584 --> 00:09:16,500
- Just look at her smile.
- She's so cute.

168
00:09:18,584 --> 00:09:20,542
Sorry. I won't look at you.

169
00:09:20,542 --> 00:09:22,417
Sorry, baby.

170
00:09:22,417 --> 00:09:24,792
Sorry, I won't look.

171
00:09:24,792 --> 00:09:26,500
I won't.

172
00:09:34,042 --> 00:09:37,918
You're a natural.
She stopped crying once she looked at you.

173
00:09:37,918 --> 00:09:41,792
Right? She usually cries
when she sees strangers.

174
00:09:41,792 --> 00:09:43,667
Do you have a child?

175
00:09:43,667 --> 00:09:46,334
No, just lots of practice.

176
00:09:47,083 --> 00:09:50,918
But why did you do that?
You have a baby to think of!

177
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:55,083
I needed the money to buy her formula.

178
00:09:55,751 --> 00:10:00,167
This is the last can.

179
00:10:00,167 --> 00:10:04,209
What about your husband and family?
Anyone to help you?

180
00:10:05,125 --> 00:10:07,083
It's just two of us.

181
00:10:07,083 --> 00:10:09,125
I was too young when I had her.

182
00:10:09,125 --> 00:10:11,626
I live on credit card debts.

183
00:10:12,292 --> 00:10:15,667
And I came to take over
my husband's debts, somehow.

184
00:10:15,667 --> 00:10:17,626
That's no reason to scam people.

185
00:10:17,626 --> 00:10:20,250
This is a proper crime!

186
00:10:20,250 --> 00:10:21,542
Shhh.

187
00:10:23,083 --> 00:10:25,500
What about her, your accomplice?

188
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:27,542
She's like me.

189
00:10:27,542 --> 00:10:30,083
I met her in an online
single mother community.

190
00:10:30,083 --> 00:10:33,250
She lives with her baby in a nearby motel.

191
00:10:44,918 --> 00:10:47,334
This will be enough
to keep her fed for a while.

192
00:10:47,334 --> 00:10:49,042
We got some food for you, too.

193
00:10:49,042 --> 00:10:50,834
You need energy after birth.

194
00:10:55,667 --> 00:10:57,000
Thank you.

195
00:10:58,709 --> 00:11:00,959
I will return the favor. I promise.

196
00:11:00,959 --> 00:11:03,959
Don't worry about it.
Just worry about the baby.

197
00:11:03,959 --> 00:11:05,667
And don't do that again.

198
00:11:05,667 --> 00:11:07,542
If you get caught scamming again,

199
00:11:07,542 --> 00:11:10,209
I'm taking you in no matter what.

200
00:11:10,209 --> 00:11:11,667
Okay.

201
00:11:12,584 --> 00:11:14,709
I won't do it again.

202
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,125
Let's go.

203
00:11:30,542 --> 00:11:32,542
How long is it gonna last?

204
00:11:32,542 --> 00:11:35,834
They can't live in motels forever.

205
00:11:35,834 --> 00:11:38,292
Well, we gave them our name cards,

206
00:11:38,292 --> 00:11:40,626
and the shelter number.

207
00:11:40,626 --> 00:11:42,167
We'll just have to see.

208
00:11:42,167 --> 00:11:44,959
They resort to crimes because

209
00:11:44,959 --> 00:11:47,334
society is not doing its job.

210
00:11:47,334 --> 00:11:50,500
I mean, what about the babies?

211
00:11:53,918 --> 00:11:55,167
Let's go, okay?

212
00:11:56,834 --> 00:11:58,292
Let's just go.

213
00:12:03,834 --> 00:12:06,876
What else did the police say?

214
00:12:06,876 --> 00:12:09,584
Yeah, they seemed nice.

215
00:12:09,584 --> 00:12:12,542
Maybe we should have turned ourselves in.

216
00:12:13,209 --> 00:12:15,375
Let's wait a little longer.

217
00:12:16,500 --> 00:12:18,709
But what if…

218
00:12:18,709 --> 00:12:21,375
the Pastor finds out?

219
00:12:22,042 --> 00:12:26,167
[International call]

220
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:42,709
[Answer the phone or your baby dies]

221
00:12:49,959 --> 00:12:52,459
[Namgang Police Station]

222
00:12:52,459 --> 00:12:55,500
Wait, Cha Yeon Ho got a new car.

223
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:56,792
Does he drive now?

224
00:12:56,792 --> 00:13:00,334
It's quite small. Is it electric?

225
00:13:00,334 --> 00:13:03,459
Too small for such a gangly dude.

226
00:13:03,459 --> 00:13:05,000
I mean, come on.

227
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,125
Black versus white.

228
00:13:07,125 --> 00:13:10,459
Old versus new. Digital versus analog.

229
00:13:10,459 --> 00:13:12,834
Exact opposites.

230
00:13:12,834 --> 00:13:16,042
He used to get around by bike.

231
00:13:16,042 --> 00:13:17,918
How long ago was that?

232
00:13:17,918 --> 00:13:21,000
You didn't see it?
You didn't see the car coming?

233
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:23,167
What do you think?

234
00:13:23,167 --> 00:13:26,751
Your fault is like… point five…

235
00:13:26,751 --> 00:13:29,667
Are you saying it's 7.5 out of 10?

236
00:13:31,042 --> 00:13:32,876
- 8.5 actually.
- What?

237
00:13:33,709 --> 00:13:36,459
It felt just like yesterday

238
00:13:36,459 --> 00:13:38,667
when he was staring me down saying 8.5.

239
00:13:38,667 --> 00:13:41,209
Now he's got a car. The kid's all grown up.

240
00:13:42,292 --> 00:13:43,834
But anyway,

241
00:13:43,834 --> 00:13:45,584
I think if I kicked it,

242
00:13:45,584 --> 00:13:48,334
I'll send it rolling down there.

243
00:13:48,334 --> 00:13:50,334
You can't. EVs are heavy.

244
00:13:50,334 --> 00:13:54,000
- I wanna have a go at it.
- Hey.

245
00:13:57,334 --> 00:14:00,000
- Run!
- Oh, come on!

246
00:14:01,417 --> 00:14:04,417
I heard Dae Se talking behind your back.

247
00:14:04,417 --> 00:14:06,375
No way.

248
00:14:06,375 --> 00:14:09,334
He said you act all too cute for your age.

249
00:14:09,334 --> 00:14:12,083
He did, right? Right?

250
00:14:12,083 --> 00:14:14,792
Where's that punk?

251
00:14:14,792 --> 00:14:20,334
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

252
00:14:20,334 --> 00:14:22,959
<i>♪ Happy birthday dear Detective Eo ♪</i>

253
00:14:22,959 --> 00:14:25,751
<i>♪ Happy birthday to you ♪</i>

254
00:14:28,584 --> 00:14:31,209
Yay!

255
00:14:31,209 --> 00:14:33,459
Happy birthday, Hyun Kyung.

256
00:14:33,459 --> 00:14:36,584
If Dae Se hadn't bought the cake,
I would have completely forgotten.

257
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:39,459
Thank you for the cake. How did you know?

258
00:14:39,459 --> 00:14:43,125
Actually, I saw it on your phone.

259
00:14:43,125 --> 00:14:46,000
Well, I still appreciate it.

260
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:47,042
Thanks.

261
00:14:47,042 --> 00:14:50,542
Hey, Investigator Cha and I paid for the cake.

262
00:14:50,542 --> 00:14:53,209
All right already.

263
00:14:53,209 --> 00:14:54,542
Thank you, Investigator Cha.

264
00:14:54,542 --> 00:14:56,500
I didn't get you a present, though.

265
00:14:56,500 --> 00:14:59,167
- If you want something, I can-
- Gold.

266
00:14:59,167 --> 00:15:01,709
24K, about this big.

267
00:15:01,709 --> 00:15:04,751
Hm. Happy birthday.

268
00:15:05,792 --> 00:15:07,834
You want a gold necklace?

269
00:15:07,834 --> 00:15:11,375
A fake for now, but pure gold in ten years.

270
00:15:12,500 --> 00:15:15,751
I'm just kidding. I don't need a present.

271
00:15:15,751 --> 00:15:18,959
As for the necklace,

272
00:15:18,959 --> 00:15:21,250
I already have a charm necklace from my Mom.

273
00:15:21,250 --> 00:15:23,125
Oh, it looks pretty.

274
00:15:23,125 --> 00:15:25,709
Cake, anyone? Captain?

275
00:15:25,709 --> 00:15:29,042
I'm good. Enjoy the cake.

276
00:15:30,542 --> 00:15:32,834
There's plenty…

277
00:16:29,209 --> 00:16:31,792
<i>Happy birthday, honey!</i>

278
00:16:31,792 --> 00:16:34,584
<i>I know you are too busy to see me,</i>

279
00:16:34,584 --> 00:16:36,834
<i>but I still wanted to give you this cake.</i>

280
00:16:36,834 --> 00:16:38,751
<i>Make a wish before you eat it,</i>

281
00:16:38,751 --> 00:16:41,167
<i>that we can spend the next birthday together.</i>

282
00:16:42,292 --> 00:16:46,417
<i>And don't skip your meals. Love, Yun Hee.</i>

283
00:17:10,375 --> 00:17:13,292
Captain, we're off.

284
00:17:13,292 --> 00:17:16,167
Someone was ran over in Samjeon Tunnel.

285
00:17:22,459 --> 00:17:25,626
What's the deal here?

286
00:17:25,626 --> 00:17:28,667
Someone ran over her.
She was lying on the floor.

287
00:17:28,667 --> 00:17:32,542
She reeked of alcohol,
and was already dead when we got here.

288
00:17:32,542 --> 00:17:34,000
Must be a stealth pedestrian.

289
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,626
This has been happening a lot lately.

290
00:17:37,626 --> 00:17:39,167
Where's the driver?

291
00:17:39,167 --> 00:17:41,000
He's here.

292
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:42,584
You two, take a look at the victim.

293
00:17:42,584 --> 00:17:44,667
Excuse me.

294
00:17:44,667 --> 00:17:46,542
The black box.

295
00:17:48,626 --> 00:17:50,000
Here.

296
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,083
It reeks of alcohol.

297
00:17:56,083 --> 00:17:59,000
[Recording]

298
00:18:03,459 --> 00:18:05,250
The lights are so dim.

299
00:18:05,250 --> 00:18:07,667
It's almost impossible
to notice her while driving.

300
00:18:07,667 --> 00:18:10,542
She popped out of nowhere.
You can't expect me not to hit her.

301
00:18:10,542 --> 00:18:13,000
It's like she had a death wish.

302
00:18:14,334 --> 00:18:17,292
But how did she get here?

303
00:18:17,292 --> 00:18:19,918
This is a motorway.

304
00:18:19,918 --> 00:18:21,959
It's not accessible for pedestrians.

305
00:18:26,334 --> 00:18:27,167
[Investigation in progress]

306
00:18:27,167 --> 00:18:28,918
Lieutenant!

307
00:18:28,918 --> 00:18:30,292
What is it?

308
00:18:30,876 --> 00:18:32,584
It's her.

309
00:18:41,334 --> 00:18:43,417
- The wrist scammer?
- Yes.

310
00:18:43,417 --> 00:18:47,209
- Wrist scam?
- She tried to scam me yesterday.

311
00:18:47,209 --> 00:18:49,751
She staged an accident

312
00:18:49,751 --> 00:18:53,542
to extort money from me, but…

313
00:18:53,542 --> 00:18:57,042
I let her go because I felt bad for her.

314
00:19:00,083 --> 00:19:02,000
The baby!

315
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:05,834
Thank you. Oh my gosh.

316
00:19:06,876 --> 00:19:09,709
Oh my god, baby!

317
00:19:09,709 --> 00:19:11,959
- I knew it. She's crying more.
- Let me take her.

318
00:19:11,959 --> 00:19:15,584
- Thank you, Hyun Kyung.
- Good girl.

319
00:19:19,000 --> 00:19:21,751
Why are you good with babies?

320
00:19:21,751 --> 00:19:22,918
Huh?

321
00:19:22,918 --> 00:19:26,876
What was she even doing there without her baby?

322
00:19:26,876 --> 00:19:28,751
And she was hammered, too!

323
00:19:28,751 --> 00:19:30,876
Maybe she couldn't take it any more.

324
00:19:30,876 --> 00:19:32,417
I mean, she struggled alone,

325
00:19:32,417 --> 00:19:35,292
without anywhere to call for help.

326
00:19:35,292 --> 00:19:36,876
If she had wanted to end it,

327
00:19:36,876 --> 00:19:39,209
this baby bottle would be empty.

328
00:19:43,959 --> 00:19:46,125
No mobile phone at the scene, right?

329
00:19:46,125 --> 00:19:47,834
Let's look for it here.

330
00:19:47,834 --> 00:19:50,083
Start looking. You watch the baby.

331
00:19:50,083 --> 00:19:51,667
[Pastor]

332
00:19:51,667 --> 00:19:53,375
Where is it?

333
00:20:23,918 --> 00:20:25,000
Who are you?

334
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:26,417
Hey.

335
00:20:28,042 --> 00:20:30,334
Hey, who are you?

336
00:20:30,334 --> 00:20:32,167
- Who are you?
- I'm sorry.

337
00:20:32,167 --> 00:20:36,125
I'm Mi Yeong's friend.
She didn't pick up her phone.

338
00:20:37,500 --> 00:20:40,667
It's okay. You can get up now. We're the police.

339
00:20:40,667 --> 00:20:42,292
Just get up.

340
00:20:42,292 --> 00:20:44,167
It's okay. Nice and slow.

341
00:20:46,959 --> 00:20:48,918
Are you hurt?

342
00:20:48,918 --> 00:20:50,375
No.

343
00:20:51,876 --> 00:20:54,626
So, her name was Kim Mi Yeong?

344
00:20:55,417 --> 00:20:57,250
That's what she told me.

345
00:20:58,209 --> 00:21:00,292
How do you know each other?

346
00:21:00,292 --> 00:21:03,042
We met in an online single mother community.

347
00:21:03,042 --> 00:21:06,792
We didn't have anyone else,
and we were in similar situations.

348
00:21:06,792 --> 00:21:08,918
Sometimes, we took turns
babysitting for each other.

349
00:21:08,918 --> 00:21:11,751
Is there anyone else you know
from the community?

350
00:21:11,751 --> 00:21:14,751
Da Eun. Park Da Eun.

351
00:21:14,751 --> 00:21:16,834
The three of us are close.

352
00:21:16,834 --> 00:21:20,459
Why were you hiding, like a suspect?

353
00:21:22,083 --> 00:21:23,500
- Wait, were you also-
- No.

354
00:21:23,500 --> 00:21:24,834
I…

355
00:21:28,083 --> 00:21:30,626
I was scared, is all.

356
00:21:30,626 --> 00:21:32,626
What do you mean, no?
I didn't even say anything.

357
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:35,375
You're being strange.

358
00:21:35,375 --> 00:21:38,959
When did you lose contact with Ms. Kim?

359
00:21:38,959 --> 00:21:41,042
Last night.

360
00:21:41,042 --> 00:21:45,083
She wouldn't answer or text me back.
So I came here looking for her.

361
00:21:45,083 --> 00:21:46,417
But there was only the baby.

362
00:21:47,459 --> 00:21:49,083
Wait,

363
00:21:49,083 --> 00:21:51,751
did something happen to her?

364
00:21:58,209 --> 00:22:01,876
Where is Mi Yeong?

365
00:22:04,292 --> 00:22:05,417
What?

366
00:22:06,959 --> 00:22:09,167
She passed away.

367
00:22:10,167 --> 00:22:11,667
Passed away?

368
00:22:12,834 --> 00:22:16,000
She was found in a tunnel this morning.

369
00:22:22,292 --> 00:22:23,834
Did she…

370
00:22:26,167 --> 00:22:28,334
did she smell of booze?

371
00:22:28,334 --> 00:22:31,000
Yes. How did you…

372
00:22:35,751 --> 00:22:39,375
[Laon's Motel]

373
00:22:51,083 --> 00:22:52,584
Just a sec.

374
00:22:52,584 --> 00:22:54,209
Where you going?

375
00:23:00,292 --> 00:23:02,042
We got a call from NFS.

376
00:23:02,042 --> 00:23:05,876
They found a wound in her head.
It's not related to the run-over.

377
00:23:05,876 --> 00:23:07,626
Another wound?

378
00:23:07,626 --> 00:23:10,500
Do we have her blood alcohol level?

379
00:23:10,500 --> 00:23:12,292
Yes, it's zero.

380
00:23:12,292 --> 00:23:14,792
What? How can it be zero?

381
00:23:14,792 --> 00:23:18,083
Investigator Cha asked me to check,
and that's the result I got.

382
00:23:20,500 --> 00:23:24,167
The accident took place in a motorway tunnel.

383
00:23:24,167 --> 00:23:27,876
I suspected it might be a homicide.

384
00:23:27,876 --> 00:23:32,125
So, someone poured booze on her clothes?

385
00:23:32,125 --> 00:23:36,209
We didn't find any CCTV footage
of her walking there.

386
00:23:36,209 --> 00:23:38,792
The booze, the head wound.

387
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:41,584
This is looking less and less like an accident.

388
00:23:41,584 --> 00:23:44,000
What we have found so far

389
00:23:44,000 --> 00:23:47,083
suggests that someone hit her in the head,

390
00:23:47,083 --> 00:23:50,500
and left her in the tunnel,

391
00:23:50,500 --> 00:23:52,709
to be run over like she was.

392
00:23:52,709 --> 00:23:55,292
All that while she was still alive.
Who would do such a thing?

393
00:23:55,292 --> 00:23:59,626
We have no CCTV footage in the tunnel.
They were replacing the cameras.

394
00:23:59,626 --> 00:24:02,125
We don't know what happened in there.

395
00:24:03,250 --> 00:24:06,125
Let's compare the footage at the exits.

396
00:24:06,125 --> 00:24:09,792
If they used a car to place Ms. Kim there,

397
00:24:09,792 --> 00:24:12,709
it would have taken unusually long
to exit the tunnel.

398
00:24:14,334 --> 00:24:17,000
Well, it looks like Dong Gi
is up for another binge session.

399
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,709
Well, I'm getting used to drying my eyes out.

400
00:24:20,709 --> 00:24:22,584
- I'll support him, sir.
- Good.

401
00:24:22,584 --> 00:24:25,167
Image analysis is traffic crime 101.

402
00:24:25,167 --> 00:24:27,042
Just watch him and learn.

403
00:24:27,042 --> 00:24:28,667
- I will, sir.
- Let's move out!

404
00:24:28,667 --> 00:24:31,459
I wonder how the baby is doing.

405
00:24:31,459 --> 00:24:35,125
Well, she's in good hands.

406
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:38,626
You've never brought your date here.

407
00:24:38,626 --> 00:24:41,542
And now you show up with a baby?
Don't you think the order is all wrong?

408
00:24:41,542 --> 00:24:44,042
Well, you did want a grandchild.

409
00:24:44,042 --> 00:24:46,542
Well,

410
00:24:46,542 --> 00:24:48,083
is she really mine?

411
00:24:48,083 --> 00:24:51,375
Well, she has my nose bridge.

412
00:24:51,375 --> 00:24:52,918
Right?

413
00:24:53,667 --> 00:24:55,667
I see the resemblance.

414
00:24:56,667 --> 00:24:59,209
When did you start making jokes?

415
00:24:59,209 --> 00:25:01,292
Dad, you look so comfy with her.

416
00:25:01,292 --> 00:25:04,584
Who do you think raised you?

417
00:25:04,584 --> 00:25:05,792
By myself, to boot!

418
00:25:05,792 --> 00:25:08,292
Yeah. It really shows.

419
00:25:09,334 --> 00:25:12,167
- So Dad, I was thinking-
- Excuse me.

420
00:25:12,167 --> 00:25:13,626
- Yes?
- Can I order now?

421
00:25:13,626 --> 00:25:15,792
Of course! Just a minute.

422
00:25:15,792 --> 00:25:17,417
Talk to me later.

423
00:25:17,417 --> 00:25:19,000
Enjoy the food.

424
00:25:19,000 --> 00:25:20,459
Thank you.

425
00:25:22,292 --> 00:25:25,459
You're really asking him
to take care of the baby?

426
00:25:25,459 --> 00:25:27,292
What else can I do?

427
00:25:27,292 --> 00:25:29,792
Kim Mi Yeong does not have anyone,

428
00:25:29,792 --> 00:25:33,042
and it takes time to find foster parents.

429
00:25:33,042 --> 00:25:34,918
Above all, she's safe here.

430
00:25:35,626 --> 00:25:37,000
That's true.

431
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:39,167
Half the customers here are cops.

432
00:25:39,167 --> 00:25:40,667
I will help when I can.

433
00:25:42,417 --> 00:25:45,292
Anyway, he's so good with the kid.

434
00:25:45,292 --> 00:25:49,459
The new director is your ex?

435
00:25:54,459 --> 00:25:56,667
Fortune finally smiles on you!

436
00:25:56,667 --> 00:25:59,876
I mean, you've been so down on your luck.

437
00:25:59,876 --> 00:26:02,167
Now, you have some strings to pull.

438
00:26:02,167 --> 00:26:04,709
Strings? Strings?

439
00:26:04,709 --> 00:26:06,751
How can you even say that?

440
00:26:06,751 --> 00:26:08,834
Don't reduce our relationship like that.

441
00:26:08,834 --> 00:26:10,542
I'm so not fine with it.

442
00:26:10,542 --> 00:26:13,876
- I didn't reduce anything!
- Just be quiet.

443
00:26:13,876 --> 00:26:16,834
Like your love is so pure, huh?

444
00:26:16,834 --> 00:26:18,459
- Oh, hello.
- You're here, Chief?

445
00:26:18,459 --> 00:26:21,000
Yes, hello. Who is this baby?

446
00:26:21,000 --> 00:26:24,417
Lieutenant Min's sister?

447
00:26:24,417 --> 00:26:28,626
- Wow, you've still got it!
- My gosh, of course not.

448
00:26:28,626 --> 00:26:30,542
My shelf life is over.

449
00:26:30,542 --> 00:26:33,292
- Come on! You embarrass me.
- Sir.

450
00:26:33,292 --> 00:26:35,918
- Yes?
- Can you help me with the gas?

451
00:26:35,918 --> 00:26:37,042
Gas?

452
00:26:37,042 --> 00:26:39,709
You go take care of it.

453
00:26:40,500 --> 00:26:42,000
Wait.

454
00:26:42,000 --> 00:26:45,792
Chief, I'll come back in a minute.

455
00:26:45,792 --> 00:26:47,834
- Yes, go ahead.
- Chief,

456
00:26:47,834 --> 00:26:50,292
- can you look after her for a bit?
- Me?

457
00:26:50,292 --> 00:26:52,792
Hey, hey!

458
00:26:52,792 --> 00:26:55,042
I won't take long.

459
00:26:55,584 --> 00:26:58,500
You really have no clue.
Just make her feel safe!

460
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:00,876
- You do it.
- Wait.

461
00:27:00,876 --> 00:27:02,876
Hey, Mom. I'm about to eat.

462
00:27:02,876 --> 00:27:04,125
Why that little…

463
00:27:04,125 --> 00:27:06,542
Rock-a-bye baby…

464
00:27:06,542 --> 00:27:09,417
Hello.

465
00:27:09,417 --> 00:27:12,125
- Is that his baby?
- Does he have a child?

466
00:27:12,125 --> 00:27:13,042
Chief? A baby?

467
00:27:13,042 --> 00:27:15,542
- Chief got divorced, you know.
- Didn't know he had a kid.

468
00:27:15,542 --> 00:27:17,500
Is that really his baby?

469
00:27:17,500 --> 00:27:20,375
How old do you think she is?

470
00:27:20,375 --> 00:27:22,500
Stop. What car is this?

471
00:27:22,500 --> 00:27:24,751
Is it… Tristar?

472
00:27:24,751 --> 00:27:26,542
Correct. Which model?

473
00:27:26,542 --> 00:27:28,000
Model? God…

474
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:30,375
E-class. C-Class has a shorter hood.

475
00:27:30,375 --> 00:27:32,626
It has vertical grills, too.

476
00:27:32,626 --> 00:27:35,709
And S-class has an emblem on the hood.

477
00:27:35,709 --> 00:27:37,417
Like, "I'm S-class."

478
00:27:38,292 --> 00:27:39,542
How do you know all that?

479
00:27:39,542 --> 00:27:42,834
You should be able to guess
the model just from pieces.

480
00:27:42,834 --> 00:27:45,709
If you can identify head lamps,
side mirrors, and bumper pieces,

481
00:27:45,709 --> 00:27:47,959
they'll tell you so much about the car.

482
00:27:47,959 --> 00:27:50,209
Do you see the side mirrors in this box?

483
00:27:50,209 --> 00:27:53,542
Memorize them until you can tell
the model right away!

484
00:27:53,542 --> 00:27:54,751
Yes, sir!

485
00:27:54,751 --> 00:27:58,125
Wow, are you teaching the new guy?

486
00:27:58,125 --> 00:27:59,584
Way to go, Dong Gi.

487
00:28:00,292 --> 00:28:03,000
Check the time stamps already!

488
00:28:03,542 --> 00:28:07,334
Yes! A black Tristar, E-class,
entered the tunnel at 6:56 a.m.

489
00:28:07,334 --> 00:28:09,918
Took 2 minutes and 12 seconds.

490
00:28:09,918 --> 00:28:12,626
It's close to the 70km/h average.

491
00:28:12,626 --> 00:28:14,292
Okay, next!

492
00:28:14,292 --> 00:28:17,459
Here's the call log from her phone.
Her last call was with Park Da Eun.

493
00:28:17,459 --> 00:28:20,000
Most calls were with her.
She also uses a prepaid phone.

494
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:23,375
- Wasn't Park Da Eun the…?
- Yes, the shill.

495
00:28:24,083 --> 00:28:27,292
Two hours before the accident,

496
00:28:27,292 --> 00:28:30,000
Park called Kim 30 times over just 30 minutes.

497
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:32,250
What made her so desperate?

498
00:28:33,209 --> 00:28:34,792
Have you contacted Park Da Eun?

499
00:28:34,792 --> 00:28:36,542
Her phone is turned off.

500
00:28:40,250 --> 00:28:42,584
Let's look for her. According to Kim Mi Yeong,

501
00:28:42,584 --> 00:28:44,375
she's at a nearby motel.

502
00:28:44,375 --> 00:28:46,083
I'm going out, Captain.

503
00:28:46,083 --> 00:28:47,083
Let's go, Dong Gi.

504
00:28:47,083 --> 00:28:48,834
See you later.

505
00:28:48,834 --> 00:28:51,417
Train him for me, sir.

506
00:28:52,083 --> 00:28:53,709
There will be a test when I get back.

507
00:28:53,709 --> 00:28:55,000
- I'll be right here, sir!
- Fighting!

508
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:56,626
- Fighting!
- Fighting!

509
00:28:57,834 --> 00:28:59,417
Which model is it?

510
00:29:00,125 --> 00:29:02,500
- Tristar?
- Elantra. Which one is this?

511
00:29:02,500 --> 00:29:05,584
- Tristar.
- Sonata. Keep working on it.

512
00:29:07,542 --> 00:29:08,876
Yes, sir.

513
00:29:12,667 --> 00:29:14,083
Excuse me.

514
00:29:14,083 --> 00:29:16,751
Have you seen this person?

515
00:29:16,751 --> 00:29:19,083
Have you seen this person?

516
00:29:19,083 --> 00:29:20,542
I don't recognize her.

517
00:29:21,250 --> 00:29:23,459
Have you seen this person?

518
00:29:23,459 --> 00:29:25,626
- No, I haven't.
- Sorry.

519
00:29:25,626 --> 00:29:27,459
Hi, have you seen this person?

520
00:29:27,459 --> 00:29:30,042
- Don't know her.
- Wait, sir!

521
00:29:31,459 --> 00:29:32,584
Park Da Eun?

522
00:29:32,584 --> 00:29:34,334
Oh my gosh.

523
00:29:37,209 --> 00:29:38,500
Hey,

524
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:43,459
you think something happened to her?

525
00:29:43,459 --> 00:29:45,876
Let's check for accident reports.

526
00:29:45,876 --> 00:29:48,500
See if there were any similar cases.

527
00:29:59,834 --> 00:30:01,500
[Pastor]

528
00:30:03,918 --> 00:30:05,209
[Pastor]

529
00:30:05,209 --> 00:30:06,959
[Pastor]

530
00:30:06,959 --> 00:30:08,584
<i>Pastor?</i>

531
00:30:11,292 --> 00:30:14,709
Park Da Eun. She was brought
to the ER this morning.

532
00:30:14,709 --> 00:30:17,292
She was lying on the road drunk
when she was ran over.

533
00:30:17,292 --> 00:30:18,626
According to the police,

534
00:30:18,626 --> 00:30:21,334
after the garbage truck driver realised,

535
00:30:21,334 --> 00:30:23,500
he called the police immediately.

536
00:30:24,042 --> 00:30:26,125
There is no one we can contact.

537
00:30:26,125 --> 00:30:28,125
We're not sure what to do.

538
00:30:28,125 --> 00:30:29,584
Is she here?

539
00:30:33,584 --> 00:30:35,417
How is she?

540
00:30:35,417 --> 00:30:36,584
Can she recover?

541
00:30:36,584 --> 00:30:39,292
Skull fracture and severe organ damage.

542
00:30:39,292 --> 00:30:43,292
If bleeding resumes or brain pressure increases,
it could be dangerous.

543
00:30:43,292 --> 00:30:45,125
We'll have to wait and see.

544
00:30:57,042 --> 00:31:00,083
Kim Mi Yeong and Park Da Eun
had similar accidents.

545
00:31:00,083 --> 00:31:03,584
The execution was the same.

546
00:31:03,584 --> 00:31:05,334
Someone made it look like

547
00:31:05,334 --> 00:31:07,959
a stealth pedestrian run-over.

548
00:31:07,959 --> 00:31:10,042
But why?

549
00:31:10,042 --> 00:31:12,959
If another single mom had conflict with them

550
00:31:12,959 --> 00:31:16,083
she would have taken a much simpler approach.

551
00:31:16,709 --> 00:31:18,334
Could it be money, then?

552
00:31:19,792 --> 00:31:23,209
But they are so broke that they scam people for…

553
00:31:25,667 --> 00:31:27,626
Life insurance money.

554
00:31:30,500 --> 00:31:33,209
We got to look into Park Da Eun's insurance.

555
00:31:33,209 --> 00:31:34,667
But how did she know?

556
00:31:35,667 --> 00:31:37,626
- Know what?
- Na Hae Ju.

557
00:31:37,626 --> 00:31:40,000
Did she smell of booze?

558
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:43,083
She knew Kim Mi Yeong's body
smelled of alcohol.

559
00:31:43,083 --> 00:31:45,000
She didn't even drink it.

560
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:48,209
Someone poured it on her clothes
to make it look like she was drunk.

561
00:31:48,209 --> 00:31:49,709
You're right.

562
00:31:49,709 --> 00:31:53,584
She asked if she smelled of booze,
not if she was drunk.

563
00:31:53,584 --> 00:31:55,000
Hold on.

564
00:31:57,709 --> 00:31:58,584
Dong Gi, what's up?

565
00:31:58,584 --> 00:32:01,125
We found the car that left
Kim Mi Yeong in the tunnel.

566
00:32:01,125 --> 00:32:05,000
Also, Kim Mi Yeong's insurance money
goes to Na Hae Ju.

567
00:32:05,000 --> 00:32:06,459
What?

568
00:32:09,876 --> 00:32:11,959
The tunnel is 1944 meters long.

569
00:32:11,959 --> 00:32:13,959
At the 70 km/h speed limit,

570
00:32:13,959 --> 00:32:16,667
most cars exit the tunnel within two minutes.

571
00:32:16,667 --> 00:32:19,250
However, this black Starline,

572
00:32:19,250 --> 00:32:22,042
- is the only car that took four minutes…
- And 28 seconds.

573
00:32:22,042 --> 00:32:24,959
Yes. 4 minutes and 28 seconds.

574
00:32:24,959 --> 00:32:26,792
The speed averages at 30 km/h.

575
00:32:26,792 --> 00:32:29,042
26 km/h to be exact.

576
00:32:29,042 --> 00:32:32,042
If they traveled at 70 km/h,

577
00:32:32,667 --> 00:32:35,459
they stopped for 2 minutes 48 seconds.

578
00:32:35,459 --> 00:32:37,542
- Wow!
- Better get used to it.

579
00:32:37,542 --> 00:32:39,042
Have you identified the number?

580
00:32:39,042 --> 00:32:41,167
Yes, luckily there was an

581
00:32:41,167 --> 00:32:45,083
[ANPR: Automatic number plate recognition]
ANPR camera at the entrance.

582
00:32:45,083 --> 00:32:47,334
It's… 23 OH 4286.

583
00:32:47,334 --> 00:32:49,417
But here's the catch.

584
00:32:49,417 --> 00:32:51,000
The owner is Kim Dong Ho.

585
00:32:51,000 --> 00:32:54,792
He gave it to a loan shark to settle a debt.

586
00:32:54,792 --> 00:32:56,792
But they didn't take over the title.

587
00:32:56,792 --> 00:32:59,667
So the car changed hands without registration.

588
00:32:59,667 --> 00:33:01,626
Probably, yes.

589
00:33:01,626 --> 00:33:03,709
But this car…

590
00:33:04,292 --> 00:33:06,584
- What about it?
- One moment.

591
00:33:11,792 --> 00:33:15,500
It's a clip of the CCTV
from the motel where Kim stayed.

592
00:33:15,500 --> 00:33:16,709
Here.

593
00:33:22,042 --> 00:33:23,584
Wait.

594
00:33:23,584 --> 00:33:26,292
Look at the plate.

595
00:33:27,459 --> 00:33:29,125
Isn't it the same car?

596
00:33:29,125 --> 00:33:31,292
- Show us more. Run it.
- Yeah.

597
00:33:39,709 --> 00:33:41,500
The car is leaving.

598
00:33:45,584 --> 00:33:47,334
Isn't that Kim Mi Yeong?

599
00:33:47,334 --> 00:33:49,167
If this is the suspect's vehicle,

600
00:33:49,167 --> 00:33:51,500
the suspect was looking for Kim Mi Yeong.

601
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:52,876
And drew her out.

602
00:34:00,417 --> 00:34:02,000
Na Hae Ju?

603
00:34:06,459 --> 00:34:08,500
Both Kim Mi Yeong and
Park Da Eun's insurance money

604
00:34:08,500 --> 00:34:10,334
- goes to Na Hae Ju.
- Na Hae Ju?

605
00:34:10,334 --> 00:34:12,584
You mean she was after the insurance money?

606
00:34:12,584 --> 00:34:13,959
[Accidental death insurance]

607
00:34:13,959 --> 00:34:15,083
[Beneficiary: Na Hae Ju]

608
00:34:15,083 --> 00:34:16,959
[Accidental death insurance
beneficiary: Na Hae Ju]

609
00:34:16,959 --> 00:34:19,751
But why would they do that for her?

610
00:34:19,751 --> 00:34:20,834
They are not even related.

611
00:34:20,834 --> 00:34:24,834
Like the Starline car owner,
both of them must have had debts.

612
00:34:24,834 --> 00:34:28,292
Some dates were marked on their calendars.

613
00:34:28,292 --> 00:34:29,959
They withdrew money on those dates.

614
00:34:29,959 --> 00:34:32,334
It went to Na Hae Ju's account.

615
00:34:32,334 --> 00:34:35,792
Does it mean Na Hae Ju is the loan shark?

616
00:34:35,792 --> 00:34:37,375
If Na Hae Ju were a friend,

617
00:34:37,375 --> 00:34:41,709
she wouldn't have made them
sign up for death insurance plans.

618
00:34:42,334 --> 00:34:43,709
Do you have her contact info?

619
00:34:43,709 --> 00:34:46,417
I got it when we met her.

620
00:34:50,250 --> 00:34:51,709
It's turned off.

621
00:34:55,209 --> 00:34:57,125
What the hell?

622
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:01,459
Come on.

623
00:35:02,125 --> 00:35:04,250
Two days, two babies.

624
00:35:04,250 --> 00:35:06,500
You can't keep doing this!

625
00:35:06,500 --> 00:35:09,918
Sorry, Dad. Just for a few days.

626
00:35:10,584 --> 00:35:14,417
Who are these kids, anyway?
Where are the parents?

627
00:35:15,042 --> 00:35:16,918
They can't be here.

628
00:35:18,292 --> 00:35:21,792
- You poor things.
- Excuse me.

629
00:35:21,792 --> 00:35:25,250
Be right there! Just a second.

630
00:35:28,709 --> 00:35:30,167
Thank you, Dad.

631
00:35:30,918 --> 00:35:33,209
- Come, have a seat.
- It's Na Hae Ju.

632
00:35:33,209 --> 00:35:35,542
She's a beneficiary
in multiple insurance policies.

633
00:35:35,542 --> 00:35:39,250
She actually got money recently. Take a look.

634
00:35:42,334 --> 00:35:44,667
There are so many.

635
00:35:44,667 --> 00:35:48,751
Most of them are in their early 20's.
Just like Kim Mi Yeong and Park Da Eun.

636
00:35:48,751 --> 00:35:50,876
Can't be sure until we check,
but they are probably

637
00:35:50,876 --> 00:35:53,626
financially related to Na Hae Ju.

638
00:35:53,626 --> 00:35:56,417
But how did they end up with Na Hae Ju?

639
00:35:56,417 --> 00:35:58,876
We'll have to look into it.

640
00:35:58,876 --> 00:36:02,500
We need to talk to these people.

641
00:36:02,500 --> 00:36:04,334
Dong Gi, Hyun Kyung,

642
00:36:04,334 --> 00:36:06,792
go find the original owner of the Starline.

643
00:36:06,792 --> 00:36:09,500
- Will do.
- Find out how the car changed hands.

644
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:11,417
- Okay.
- Okay.

645
00:36:13,167 --> 00:36:14,584
Pastor…

646
00:36:15,292 --> 00:36:17,792
You go to church now?

647
00:36:17,792 --> 00:36:19,125
No.

648
00:36:20,626 --> 00:36:23,959
- Hello.
- Come on.

649
00:36:35,542 --> 00:36:37,751
Just look at this.

650
00:36:37,751 --> 00:36:39,542
What are they even doing with my car?

651
00:36:39,542 --> 00:36:42,375
I get tickets practically every day.

652
00:36:42,375 --> 00:36:45,292
Illegal parking speeding,
traffic light violation.

653
00:36:45,292 --> 00:36:49,000
This loan shark made my life a living hell.

654
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:52,542
Did they give you a business card
or any contact information?

655
00:36:52,542 --> 00:36:55,667
Do you think they even bothered?

656
00:36:55,667 --> 00:36:57,459
They just barged in and…

657
00:36:57,459 --> 00:36:58,918
Did you see their faces?

658
00:36:58,918 --> 00:37:00,500
Faces?

659
00:37:00,500 --> 00:37:03,250
They looked like him.

660
00:37:03,250 --> 00:37:04,584
Huh?

661
00:37:05,584 --> 00:37:07,667
- Me?
- Yes.

662
00:37:07,667 --> 00:37:09,209
Me?

663
00:37:09,209 --> 00:37:10,918
[Administrative fine notice]

664
00:37:10,918 --> 00:37:12,959
I mean, your physique.

665
00:37:12,959 --> 00:37:14,500
They looked like me?

666
00:37:14,500 --> 00:37:16,000
No, I mean,

667
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:18,417
not exactly like you.

668
00:37:18,417 --> 00:37:20,292
You forgot your glasses?

669
00:37:20,292 --> 00:37:23,334
I don't wear glasses. I have 20-20 vision.

670
00:37:23,334 --> 00:37:25,459
[Parking violation notice]

671
00:37:27,167 --> 00:37:29,667
Let me help you.

672
00:37:30,834 --> 00:37:32,000
Who are you?

673
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:34,042
Police. Don't worry.

674
00:37:34,042 --> 00:37:37,083
We just have some questions.

675
00:37:46,918 --> 00:37:49,250
Could we talk in the car?

676
00:37:52,375 --> 00:37:54,000
All right.

677
00:37:55,250 --> 00:37:58,417
- Where's the baby?
- She's asleep.

678
00:37:59,834 --> 00:38:03,751
How do you know Na Hae Ju?

679
00:38:03,751 --> 00:38:08,250
I saw a post for a job
in the single mom community.

680
00:38:08,250 --> 00:38:10,083
It said I just need an insurance.

681
00:38:10,083 --> 00:38:12,500
It said it was easy money.

682
00:38:13,667 --> 00:38:15,459
What was the job?

683
00:38:15,459 --> 00:38:17,375
- "Mannequin."
- Mannequin?

684
00:38:17,375 --> 00:38:18,709
[Mannequin: A passenger involved
in a staged accident scam]

685
00:38:18,709 --> 00:38:21,375
You mean, the one where you
stage an accident to get money?

686
00:38:21,375 --> 00:38:22,375
"Rear-end fraud"?

687
00:38:22,375 --> 00:38:24,292
[Rear-end fraud: Deliberately crashing
from the back for insurance money]

688
00:38:24,292 --> 00:38:26,334
I know what I did was wrong.

689
00:38:26,334 --> 00:38:29,918
But I couldn't get a job because of the kid.

690
00:38:29,918 --> 00:38:32,292
And I needed the money.

691
00:38:32,292 --> 00:38:34,375
So I did it anyway.

692
00:38:35,125 --> 00:38:37,167
I'm sorry.

693
00:38:38,167 --> 00:38:40,417
Then, about Na Hae Ju…

694
00:38:40,918 --> 00:38:43,417
I met her while doing the mannequin gig.

695
00:38:44,375 --> 00:38:48,375
We had a lot in common.

696
00:38:48,375 --> 00:38:51,667
When I told her I was broke,
she hooked me up with a lender.

697
00:38:51,667 --> 00:38:53,834
- And…
- It was a loan shark.

698
00:38:54,626 --> 00:38:57,250
When I couldn't pay back, some scary dudes came

699
00:38:57,250 --> 00:38:58,751
and forced me to sign.

700
00:38:58,751 --> 00:39:00,459
Said they'd kill me if I didn't.

701
00:39:00,459 --> 00:39:03,751
I didn't even know what I was signing.

702
00:39:03,751 --> 00:39:05,500
Have you…

703
00:39:07,209 --> 00:39:09,959
heard about the Pastor?

704
00:39:09,959 --> 00:39:11,542
Pastor?

705
00:39:14,417 --> 00:39:16,042
I don't think so.

706
00:39:17,042 --> 00:39:20,334
Oh, that post about the job?

707
00:39:20,334 --> 00:39:23,000
The writer's ID was Happy Pastor.

708
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:25,584
Happy… Pastor?

709
00:39:32,500 --> 00:39:35,834
[High-paying job opportunity]
This community has over 3,000 members.

710
00:39:35,834 --> 00:39:37,918
Advertising posts are banned here,

711
00:39:37,918 --> 00:39:41,626
but people use the anonymous forum
to post them for short periods.

712
00:39:41,626 --> 00:39:45,834
Like guerillas, they go around
online forums to upload posts.

713
00:39:45,834 --> 00:39:48,000
Earn 30 big ones on the spot?

714
00:39:48,000 --> 00:39:49,834
Talk about easy money.

715
00:39:49,834 --> 00:39:53,459
I checked Kim Mi Yeong
and Park Da Eun's insurance records.

716
00:39:54,459 --> 00:39:56,792
Over the last two years,
Kim Mi Yeong received money five times.

717
00:39:56,792 --> 00:39:58,542
Park Da Eun received money four times.

718
00:39:58,542 --> 00:40:00,542
All of them for crash accidents.

719
00:40:00,542 --> 00:40:02,459
In three of the cases, they filed claims

720
00:40:02,459 --> 00:40:05,250
for the same accident on the same day.

721
00:40:05,250 --> 00:40:08,250
Wow. All of the cars are rentals.

722
00:40:08,250 --> 00:40:11,500
Five passengers for sedans,

723
00:40:11,500 --> 00:40:13,250
nine passengers for vans.

724
00:40:13,250 --> 00:40:16,334
Each car was packed full.
Typical "rear-end" scam.

725
00:40:16,334 --> 00:40:19,500
So, both of them met Na Hae Ju
while doing the mannequin job-

726
00:40:19,500 --> 00:40:22,000
And got hooked up with a loan shark.

727
00:40:22,000 --> 00:40:24,292
It must have been their plan.

728
00:40:25,292 --> 00:40:26,918
What about the Starline?

729
00:40:26,918 --> 00:40:29,292
Nothing but a bunch of tickets.

730
00:40:29,292 --> 00:40:32,334
They don't care because the car
is not registered to them.

731
00:40:32,334 --> 00:40:34,834
The owner is going crazy over this.

732
00:40:35,584 --> 00:40:40,209
So, the "rear-end" scam serves
as a gateway to illegal loans.

733
00:40:45,292 --> 00:40:47,876
How about we do some part-time jobs ourselves?

734
00:40:50,584 --> 00:40:52,792
These jobs pay good money.

735
00:40:52,792 --> 00:40:55,417
I'm all for it. I've done many jobs.

736
00:40:55,417 --> 00:40:58,459
We used to put our hands like this.

737
00:41:06,459 --> 00:41:08,083
Don't get nervous. It's nothing.

738
00:41:08,083 --> 00:41:10,375
It's okay to quit if you can't handle it.

739
00:41:10,375 --> 00:41:11,959
I'm not that nervous.

740
00:41:11,959 --> 00:41:15,417
Good, we are just here for a part time job.

741
00:41:15,417 --> 00:41:16,751
Okay?

742
00:41:17,459 --> 00:41:19,584
Hey, what are you eating?

743
00:41:19,584 --> 00:41:21,918
Something to calm my nerves. Do you want one?

744
00:41:21,918 --> 00:41:23,459
No, I'm good.

745
00:41:29,375 --> 00:41:31,709
I almost had it.

746
00:41:32,792 --> 00:41:34,125
[Will notify time and place later]

747
00:41:34,125 --> 00:41:35,792
[Place: Haeoreum Park]

748
00:41:36,918 --> 00:41:38,667
[Place: Haeoreum Park]

749
00:41:42,959 --> 00:41:44,918
Check your bodycams.

750
00:41:44,918 --> 00:41:46,751
Okay.

751
00:41:46,751 --> 00:41:48,792
Don't get nervous.

752
00:41:48,792 --> 00:41:50,792
Split up. Act natural.

753
00:41:50,792 --> 00:41:53,459
Let's see you at the meetup.

754
00:41:58,792 --> 00:42:00,959
You'll get your phones later.

755
00:42:04,500 --> 00:42:05,626
Mannequin?

756
00:42:05,626 --> 00:42:10,042
You gotta be on time! You're ten minutes late!

757
00:42:10,042 --> 00:42:11,918
- License and phone.
- Huh?

758
00:42:11,918 --> 00:42:14,292
To make sure you're not recording.

759
00:42:14,292 --> 00:42:15,334
Oh.

760
00:42:17,209 --> 00:42:18,626
Here.

761
00:42:27,459 --> 00:42:28,834
Now, folks,

762
00:42:28,834 --> 00:42:31,375
we will split you up into offence and defense.

763
00:42:31,375 --> 00:42:33,751
Stand here if you can take some hit.

764
00:42:33,751 --> 00:42:36,584
Stand there if you like hurting people.

765
00:42:40,500 --> 00:42:42,709
Hey, you there with glasses.

766
00:42:42,709 --> 00:42:44,125
Come here.

767
00:42:46,250 --> 00:42:48,876
You don't look that tough.

768
00:42:52,500 --> 00:42:55,751
Get in here.

769
00:42:55,751 --> 00:43:00,250
Anyone up for some action?

770
00:43:03,751 --> 00:43:06,584
The driver gets 50,000 won more.

771
00:43:07,167 --> 00:43:10,167
Make it 100,000 won! Anyone?

772
00:43:12,709 --> 00:43:14,334
Hey there, latecomer!

773
00:43:14,334 --> 00:43:16,626
You've got the physique. You drive.

774
00:43:17,459 --> 00:43:19,042
Me?

775
00:43:19,042 --> 00:43:20,959
Don't back off now. You'll get more money.

776
00:43:20,959 --> 00:43:23,709
- I'm not ready to…
- You will be.

777
00:43:23,709 --> 00:43:26,125
You'll be ready when you start the car.

778
00:43:26,876 --> 00:43:28,959
All right.

779
00:43:28,959 --> 00:43:30,459
Move now.

780
00:43:36,751 --> 00:43:38,626
I'm not sure about this.

781
00:43:40,751 --> 00:43:44,167
Is he gonna be all right?
What if it gets out of hand?

782
00:43:48,667 --> 00:43:51,417
Okay, let's do it.

783
00:43:51,417 --> 00:43:52,834
When the car takes a turn,

784
00:43:52,834 --> 00:43:55,834
ram into it the moment the car changes lanes.

785
00:43:56,709 --> 00:43:58,083
Loosen up a little.

786
00:43:58,083 --> 00:43:59,542
Okay.

787
00:44:14,167 --> 00:44:17,125
All right, slowly,

788
00:44:17,125 --> 00:44:20,792
follow the car.

789
00:44:20,792 --> 00:44:23,209
Ram it, ram it, ram it!

790
00:44:26,918 --> 00:44:30,125
I said ram it, goddamn it!

791
00:44:31,083 --> 00:44:32,834
What?

792
00:44:41,500 --> 00:44:43,584
[Police]

793
00:44:46,709 --> 00:44:48,375
What in the-?

794
00:44:49,626 --> 00:44:51,459
Step out.

795
00:44:51,459 --> 00:44:53,292
I… I'm not…

796
00:44:53,292 --> 00:44:55,500
What…

797
00:44:55,500 --> 00:44:58,375
Hey, hey!

798
00:44:58,375 --> 00:45:00,083
I'm not! I'm…

799
00:45:04,167 --> 00:45:05,709
You got the wrong…

800
00:45:05,709 --> 00:45:07,500
Shut your mouth!

801
00:45:13,751 --> 00:45:15,334
Shouldn't we,

802
00:45:15,334 --> 00:45:16,626
Shouldn't we head out?

803
00:45:16,626 --> 00:45:18,459
No, we can't.

804
00:45:18,459 --> 00:45:20,209
That'll blow our cover.

805
00:45:21,918 --> 00:45:24,834
Huh? Where's Detective Eo?

806
00:45:29,459 --> 00:45:30,876
<i>Where are you?</i>

807
00:45:30,876 --> 00:45:34,250
<i>I'm still with them. Talk to you later.</i>

808
00:45:44,959 --> 00:45:46,209
Get out.

809
00:45:46,209 --> 00:45:48,751
We blew it. Just go home.

810
00:45:51,209 --> 00:45:54,667
What are you waiting for? Go!

811
00:46:14,042 --> 00:46:17,334
What are you doing here?

812
00:46:17,334 --> 00:46:18,709
You can't do this to us.

813
00:46:18,709 --> 00:46:22,083
We did everything you told us.
We can't just go home.

814
00:46:22,083 --> 00:46:24,125
What do you want?

815
00:46:24,125 --> 00:46:26,292
Pay up, or else.

816
00:46:26,292 --> 00:46:27,918
Or what?

817
00:46:27,918 --> 00:46:29,250
Give us work.

818
00:46:31,334 --> 00:46:33,959
Just go while you still can.

819
00:46:39,834 --> 00:46:41,292
What are you doing?

820
00:46:42,125 --> 00:46:45,334
Give me a ride, at least.

821
00:46:57,375 --> 00:47:00,375
Who ratted us out?

822
00:47:06,125 --> 00:47:07,417
Hey.

823
00:47:09,083 --> 00:47:12,250
Hey!

824
00:47:12,250 --> 00:47:14,125
Your driving's pretty amateur.

825
00:47:14,918 --> 00:47:17,125
- What?
- You're a cop!

826
00:47:17,125 --> 00:47:18,918
- No.
- You're a cop, aren't you?

827
00:47:18,918 --> 00:47:20,626
Who you calling a cop?

828
00:47:20,626 --> 00:47:22,959
Just pay me already.

829
00:47:26,751 --> 00:47:30,250
Min So Hee, Cha Yeon Ho,
Ji Dae Se, you're out.

830
00:47:35,959 --> 00:47:39,250
What?

831
00:47:44,584 --> 00:47:47,000
You haven't done undercover before?

832
00:47:47,000 --> 00:47:48,500
Bunch of amateurs.

833
00:47:48,500 --> 00:47:51,876
Well, I bet you don't do undercover at TCI.

834
00:47:53,125 --> 00:47:57,209
Why didn't you say you're a cop?

835
00:47:57,209 --> 00:48:00,042
I tried to, but you told me to…

836
00:48:01,375 --> 00:48:04,417
You do everything cops tell you to?

837
00:48:04,417 --> 00:48:06,417
Who are you, anyway?

838
00:48:06,417 --> 00:48:09,834
At least share your name with fellow cops.

839
00:48:16,918 --> 00:48:19,584
I don't do that,

840
00:48:20,667 --> 00:48:22,417
Lieutenant Min.

841
00:48:24,542 --> 00:48:26,000
Investigator Cha,

842
00:48:30,834 --> 00:48:32,751
and you, I don't know.

843
00:48:32,751 --> 00:48:34,626
I asked who you are.

844
00:48:34,626 --> 00:48:36,459
- Lieutenant!
- Hey.

845
00:48:36,459 --> 00:48:37,584
- Dong Gi.
- Hello.

846
00:48:37,584 --> 00:48:40,042
- Are you okay?
- Yup.

847
00:48:40,042 --> 00:48:41,500
Are you okay?

848
00:48:41,500 --> 00:48:42,876
Now, guys,

849
00:48:42,876 --> 00:48:45,834
save your family reunion for later.

850
00:48:45,834 --> 00:48:48,250
Let's talk somewhere.

851
00:48:50,250 --> 00:48:52,751
- Who is that?
- I don't know.

852
00:49:02,834 --> 00:49:04,667
Get out.

853
00:49:04,667 --> 00:49:06,417
Where are we?

854
00:49:07,167 --> 00:49:08,709
You live in Seoul, right?

855
00:49:09,459 --> 00:49:10,959
It's Seoul.

856
00:49:10,959 --> 00:49:13,417
I see.

857
00:49:13,417 --> 00:49:15,083
Thank you.

858
00:49:17,375 --> 00:49:18,751
Hey!

859
00:49:20,876 --> 00:49:22,542
Call me if you need money.

860
00:49:23,459 --> 00:49:24,792
All right.

861
00:49:30,792 --> 00:49:32,542
[Same-Day Loan]

862
00:49:38,417 --> 00:49:41,125
Shinjeon-ro 60gil.

863
00:49:43,584 --> 00:49:46,334
[Place of violation: Shinjeon-ro 60gil]

864
00:49:47,417 --> 00:49:49,250
[Anjail Car Rental]

865
00:49:49,250 --> 00:49:51,500
Car rental.

866
00:50:01,918 --> 00:50:03,667
Take a seat, everyone.

867
00:50:10,209 --> 00:50:12,459
It's been a while, Min So Hee.

868
00:50:14,459 --> 00:50:16,834
I heard you've been assigned here.

869
00:50:20,334 --> 00:50:23,167
It's been too long, Captain Jung.

870
00:50:23,167 --> 00:50:25,334
So it has been, Ma'am.

871
00:50:25,334 --> 00:50:27,334
- Pleased to work with you.
- Yes, Ma'am.

872
00:50:31,959 --> 00:50:34,042
He's Superintendent Myeong Heon Jo.

873
00:50:34,042 --> 00:50:38,167
He worked with me at Busan Narcotics.

874
00:50:38,167 --> 00:50:41,334
He may not look like much,
but he gets the job done.

875
00:50:41,334 --> 00:50:43,709
You'll be seeing him a lot around here.

876
00:50:43,709 --> 00:50:48,500
"May not look like much"?
What's wrong with how I look?

877
00:50:51,918 --> 00:50:54,834
She said hello for me, so there you go.

878
00:50:54,834 --> 00:50:57,375
Now, let's get to the point.

879
00:50:59,834 --> 00:51:01,167
A few days ago,

880
00:51:01,167 --> 00:51:03,834
Financial Supervisory Service
received an anonymous report.

881
00:51:03,834 --> 00:51:06,292
It was about an organization involved in

882
00:51:06,292 --> 00:51:08,542
insurance fraud, illegal loans, and illegal cars.

883
00:51:08,542 --> 00:51:12,500
They requested an investigation,

884
00:51:12,500 --> 00:51:15,292
and I ended up taking it as my first case here.

885
00:51:15,292 --> 00:51:17,250
We did our own research.

886
00:51:17,250 --> 00:51:19,292
They recruit people with rear-end scams,

887
00:51:19,292 --> 00:51:21,667
they hook them up with loan sharks,

888
00:51:21,667 --> 00:51:25,500
milk them dry and, lastly,
take their death insurance money.

889
00:51:26,709 --> 00:51:29,667
[Leader: Pastor]
The organization is led by…

890
00:51:29,667 --> 00:51:32,876
[Insurance: Ah Ju Im, Used Cars: Mag Sa Jang]
someone called the "Pastor".

891
00:51:33,459 --> 00:51:37,792
Black Starline, 23 OH 4286.

892
00:51:41,417 --> 00:51:44,584
Have you identified the Pastor?

893
00:51:44,584 --> 00:51:47,459
This is one thorough dude.

894
00:51:47,459 --> 00:51:49,626
All contacts are made through

895
00:51:49,626 --> 00:51:52,792
Telegram, dark web, and anonymous accounts.

896
00:51:52,792 --> 00:51:56,250
They transfer money by dead drops,
like drug dealers do.

897
00:51:56,250 --> 00:51:59,792
The money is split across dummy accounts,

898
00:51:59,792 --> 00:52:01,918
making it difficult to track them.

899
00:52:01,918 --> 00:52:03,918
All we know is the alias.

900
00:52:03,918 --> 00:52:07,375
The "Pastor".

901
00:52:07,375 --> 00:52:10,542
No one knows the face or the real name.

902
00:52:10,542 --> 00:52:13,834
Several people have died because of these frauds.

903
00:52:13,834 --> 00:52:15,167
That is why

904
00:52:15,167 --> 00:52:18,918
we were tracking the Pastor's money man,

905
00:52:20,042 --> 00:52:23,584
until you showed up and
screwed up the whole operation.

906
00:52:23,584 --> 00:52:26,167
Our operations went south as well.

907
00:52:26,167 --> 00:52:29,292
- We were tracking Na Hae Ju-
- Na Hae Ju?

908
00:52:31,000 --> 00:52:34,459
She is one of the Pastor candidates

909
00:52:34,459 --> 00:52:35,834
that we've been chasing.

910
00:52:40,751 --> 00:52:42,292
Where's Hyun Kyung?

911
00:52:43,209 --> 00:52:46,292
She called. She's still with
one of the gang members.

912
00:52:46,292 --> 00:52:47,792
She'll keep in touch.

913
00:52:47,792 --> 00:52:50,375
- Will she be okay?
- Well.

914
00:53:05,209 --> 00:53:06,834
4286.

915
00:53:08,709 --> 00:53:10,209
The cop?

916
00:53:12,792 --> 00:53:14,250
Na Hae Ju?

917
00:53:19,667 --> 00:53:21,250
She's not picking up?

918
00:53:22,209 --> 00:53:25,083
Want me to track her location?

919
00:53:26,042 --> 00:53:27,500
Let's do that.

920
00:53:27,500 --> 00:53:28,959
Yeah, do that.

921
00:53:30,584 --> 00:53:32,709
Hold on. I'll get it.

922
00:53:33,751 --> 00:53:35,751
Yes, TCI here.

923
00:53:36,459 --> 00:53:37,876
Huh? Okay.

924
00:53:38,542 --> 00:53:40,334
We'll be right there.

925
00:53:41,417 --> 00:53:44,417
They found the suspect car
used to dump Kim Mi Yeong.

926
00:53:56,876 --> 00:53:58,250
Sir.

927
00:53:58,250 --> 00:54:01,500
Looks like it fell from the overpass.
Cause of accident unknown.

928
00:54:01,500 --> 00:54:04,125
You said a body was in the car.
Have you identified it?

929
00:54:04,125 --> 00:54:08,834
Looks like a female,
but the body is completely burned.

930
00:54:08,834 --> 00:54:10,209
God…

931
00:54:12,584 --> 00:54:14,083
Is this the one?

932
00:54:14,083 --> 00:54:16,459
Yeah, 4286.

933
00:54:16,459 --> 00:54:19,250
This is the car used to dump Kim Mi Yeong.

934
00:54:35,042 --> 00:54:36,542
What is it?

935
00:54:40,375 --> 00:54:41,876
This is…

936
00:54:44,292 --> 00:54:46,417
As for the necklace,

937
00:54:46,417 --> 00:54:48,834
I already have a charm necklace from my Mom.

938
00:54:48,834 --> 00:54:50,209
Pretty, right?

939
00:54:53,500 --> 00:54:56,667
It's Detective Eo's necklace.

940
00:55:14,709 --> 00:55:16,334
Hyun Kyung…

941
00:55:23,584 --> 00:55:26,751
[National Forensic Service]
We have the result from

942
00:55:26,751 --> 00:55:28,751
the criminal DNA database.

943
00:55:30,209 --> 00:55:31,667
Take a look.

944
00:55:34,167 --> 00:55:36,709
[Comparative DNA Profile. STR Profile Obtained]
Here.

945
00:55:42,209 --> 00:55:44,250
Fancy meeting you here, Captain.

946
00:55:45,417 --> 00:55:47,459
What are you doing here?

947
00:55:47,459 --> 00:55:49,834
Why do cops come to NFS?

948
00:55:49,834 --> 00:55:53,125
I'm here for analysis results.
What about you, Captain?

949
00:55:54,751 --> 00:55:56,334
Same here.

950
00:55:59,667 --> 00:56:01,292
I'll excuse myself, then.

951
00:56:10,918 --> 00:56:12,500
Here.

952
00:56:15,083 --> 00:56:18,083
[Profile clearly matches the DNA]

953
00:56:19,292 --> 00:56:21,500
Do we have a match?

954
00:56:21,500 --> 00:56:25,334
Yes. But we haven't identified who.

955
00:56:25,334 --> 00:56:29,709
It's DNA from another cold case.

956
00:56:30,375 --> 00:56:31,918
Which case?

957
00:56:31,918 --> 00:56:35,918
A drug-related death at a club three years ago.

958
00:56:36,792 --> 00:56:39,000
The lead investigator was…

959
00:56:39,000 --> 00:56:41,083
Senior Superintendent Lee Tae Ju.

960
00:56:43,375 --> 00:56:46,375
A drug-related death?

961
00:56:47,751 --> 00:56:50,000
The illegal taxi case three years ago.

962
00:56:50,000 --> 00:56:53,959
My team went after the largest
illegal taxi ring in Gangnam.

963
00:56:53,959 --> 00:56:57,584
We obtained the leader's mobile phone,

964
00:56:57,584 --> 00:56:59,375
and found evidence of drug trafficking

965
00:56:59,375 --> 00:57:04,542
involving celebrities, doctors,
lawyers, and many others.

966
00:57:04,542 --> 00:57:06,000
I heard about it.

967
00:57:06,000 --> 00:57:08,959
The case that went cold
after Lee Tae Ju took over.

968
00:57:14,709 --> 00:57:16,375
Lee Tae Ju.

969
00:58:08,042 --> 00:58:09,709
What are you talking about?

970
00:58:09,709 --> 00:58:11,876
The burnt corpse could be Hyun Kyung?

971
00:58:11,876 --> 00:58:15,125
If Detective Eo identified the Pastor,

972
00:58:15,125 --> 00:58:18,125
what would the Pastor have done to her?

973
00:58:18,125 --> 00:58:20,500
Black Forbidden, last digits 1139.

974
00:58:20,500 --> 00:58:22,500
Heading west on local roads.

975
00:58:25,250 --> 00:58:26,667
Where's Eo Hyun Kyung!

976
00:58:26,667 --> 00:58:28,000
It's in the black box video,
and I figured it out.

977
00:58:28,000 --> 00:58:29,918
What do we do? Fight? Run?

978
00:58:29,918 --> 00:58:32,626
Police don't run!
We gotta find Hyun Kyung!

979
00:58:32,626 --> 00:58:34,292
Take this!
